# Day 43/50 — Encryption

Imagine writing a message that only the intended person can understand.
Even if someone else gets hold of it, the actual meaning remains hidden.

That's the basic idea behind **Encryption**

It converts readable information, called plaintext, into an unreadable form called ciphertext using an encryption method and a key.

Only someone with the appropriate key can decrypt it and recover the original information.
From online banking to private conversations, encryption helps protect sensitive data.

And there's something beautiful about this idea.

Not everything needs to be visible to everyone. 
Some things deserve protection, even while travelling through an open world.

**Because privacy isn't about hiding everything. It's about choosing who gets to see what.**
